        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox for Android 158 adds support for the aria-busy state; see <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=908042\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=908042</a>. AFAICT, support on desktop has been available for a long time; see <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Firefox/Releases/3/WAI_ARIA_Live_Regions_API_Support\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Firefox/Releases/3/WAI_ARIA_Live_Regions_API_Support</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a rel note for this new addition. It is a bit of a weird one — I didn't think that it should just be put in the HTML section, so I added an accessibility section. Does this seem to make sense?</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617199805\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45886\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45886/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45886\">#45886</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46025",
            "title": "Add rel note for FxA 158 aria-busy support",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-07T17:45:55.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-07T17:44:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 158 adds support for the WebGPU <code class=\"notranslate\">float32-blendable</code> feature. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1931630\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1931630</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds an appropriate note to the Firefox 158 rel notes.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617208477\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45891\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45891/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45891\">#45891</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
