        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89024979?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The \"Porting from C/C++\" section of the WebAssembly concepts guide recommends WasmFiddle++ and WasmExplorer, but neither works anymore because their shared backend service (<code class=\"notranslate\">wasmexplorer-service.herokuapp.com</code>) is gone. This replaces them with <a href=\"https://godbolt.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Compiler Explorer</a>, which can still compile C or C++ to Wasm in the browser with Clang and <code class=\"notranslate\">--target=wasm32</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #46022.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5747726227\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46022\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/46022/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46022\">#46022</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46023",
            "title": "Replace dead online Wasm assembler links in Wasm concepts guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-07T20:08:45.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-07T16:28:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "SatvikMishra08",
                "url": "https://github.com/SatvikMishra08"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 158 ships support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">Notification.navigate</code> property, which also includes the <code class=\"notranslate\">navigate</code> option of the <code class=\"notranslate\">Notification()</code> constructor and <code class=\"notranslate\">ServiceWorkerRegistration.showNotification()</code> method. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2069920\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2069920</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a rel note to cover this addition.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617222240\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45900\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45900/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45900\">#45900</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46021",
            "title": "Add Fx rel note for Notification.navigate",
