        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 158 prefs on support for on-device speech recognition in Nightly only; see <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2069803\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2069803</a>. I've tested it, and this seems to be the case: it works by default in Nightly 159, but doesn't work in Beta 158 unless you flip on the <code class=\"notranslate\">media.webspeech.recognition.enable</code> pref.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a rel note and an experimental features entry for the change.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617220730\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45899\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45899/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45899\">#45899</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
