        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is basically <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3447591712\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41267\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41267/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41267\">#41267</a>, rebased on the current docs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Since I made <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3447591712\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41267\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41267/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41267\">#41267</a>, the notifications docs have acknowledged the difference between persistent and non-persistent notifications, but I thought there was still some clarity that could be added, and some errors still (e.g. persistent notifications are <strong>not</strong> only created from a SW, they can also be created by a web page).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One thing I wasn't sure about was whether <code class=\"notranslate\">click</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">close</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">show</code> are only fired on NP notifications.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Coming back to this PR, I remember why I stalled last time: the guide page <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Notifications_API/Using_the_Notifications_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Notifications_API/Using_the_Notifications_API</a> needs a complete rewrite with new examples. I think the to-do list example is much too complex - I shouldn't have to understand IndexedDB to understand notifications.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm not proposing to do that in this PR, in the interests of finally getting it merged. But we need to do it.</p>",
