        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89024979?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates the <code class=\"notranslate\">size=\"1\"</code> paragraph in the \"Accessibility concerns\" section of the <code class=\"notranslate\">multiple</code> attribute page. It no longer tells authors never to use <code class=\"notranslate\">size=\"1\"</code> on a multiple select, since that's now the opt-in for a drop-down multi-select. It still mentions the old behavior in browsers that haven't shipped this yet, and keeps the advice to tell users that more than one option can be selected.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The page currently says \"Don't do that\" about <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;select multiple size=\"1\"&gt;</code>, which contradicts the newer HTML behavior where this markup gives a drop-down multi-select.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>HTML spec change: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3237039065\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11460\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/11460/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11460\">whatwg/html#11460</a></li>\n<li>Chrome Status: <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5412736871825408\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5412736871825408</a></li>\n<li>Firefox: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1988022\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1988022</a>, WebKit: <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=309606\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=309606</a> (and <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5665134031\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/issues/75555\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WebKit/WebKit/pull/75555/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/75555\">WebKit/WebKit#75555</a> for macOS)</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I kept the sentence about browsers without support because of the interop question in the issue. Happy to drop it and just remove the paragraph if you'd prefer.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45988.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5720172588\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45988\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45988/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45988\">#45988</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45990",
            "title": "Update size=\"1\" note for multiple select",
